If the function… Use is an internal helper you call yourself 1 — document, don't check receives user input, file data, or <code>sys.argv</code> 2 — guard clauses that raise converts text to a number or looks something up 3 — try and handle accepts human-typed text 4 — normalise, then 2 or 3 <p>These combine. A realistic boundary function normalises, tries the conversion, and guards the range:</p> <pre><code>def parse_percentage(text):
    """Return an int 0-100 parsed from `text`."""
    try:
        value = int(text.strip())
    except ValueError:
        raise ValueError(f"not a whole number: {text!r}") from None
    if not 0 &lt;= value &lt;= 100:
        raise ValueError(f"percentage must be 0-100, got {value}")
    return value
</code></pre>
